Summary: Need Nastier Monsters
Keywords: Smarts for monsters!


Speaking somewhat philosophically, one of the reasons that nethack is
hard at the beginning levels and gets very easy once you have an advanced
character, is just that there are many many items that leverage your
character.  Nethack has all these neat items, which is one of the nice
features, but the problem is that these neat items make your character
very very powerful once he gets them.  The leverage is too high; the
monsters increase more or less linearly in nastiness but the character
growth (as someone here remarked previously) is more on the exponential
side.

To keep parity and make Nethack as exciting as Rogue used to be on the
lower levels, it is _essential_ that monsters be given the same sort of
leverage.   It should be standard that an orc on level 13 or so has on
the average a +4 scimitar, +3 banded mail and hard iron boots, and so on.
After all, presumably they can (fictively) run around blessing enchant
weapon scrolls the same way you do.

Furthermore, can't we give them useful spells and let them use wands?
Let them wear magic-resistant cloaks and speed boots, occasionally give
them an amulet of reflection?  Use luckstones?  Potions of invisibility?

I think if Nethack is going to grow in a fruitful direction, the only
way we can really justify new features and keep the game balance is to
give the monsters and the players orthogonality as to what they can and
do use.

In the end this will have to involve at least a sprinkling of AI, some
judgement on the part of monsters as to what they will do.  For example,
should a demon lord follow you as you, hasted, do a hit-move twostep and
chop him to death?  Why not have monsters decide that if whatever they
are doing is not working very well, they should try some alternative
(depending on their INT rating).  The monster could easily keep track
of how much it has hit you as compared to how closely it resembles
hamburger itself.

The last time the subject of orthogonal behavior came up, somebody said, 
"The kobold zaps his wand of death.  You die."  Well, I don't think that 
would have to be a problem.
Suggestions:
Super powerful items such as a wand of death might be banned.  (I don't 
like this solution very much).
Likelihood of monsters having such powerful items on starting levels
would be very low.  For deeper levels, the player would likely
a) have a good saving throw
b) have a cloak of magic resistance or reflection or whatever.
Low level and stupid monsters like kobolds don't use powerful items very well.
Now and then (very occasionally) a shocking and sudden death when carelessly
slamming a pitiful innocent kobold would be appropriate.  A dungeon crawl
through Yendor isn't a walk in the garden!

